From de3d2941f25ebb4ab5f17b02cafa2f93cdf4fbab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:50:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] runtime: OXRSYS_FRAME_XBOX lays the Frame's controllers
 out for Touch-to-Xbox apps (UEVR)

UEVR turns Touch into an Xbox pad (right a = A, left x = B, right b = X,
left y = Y, squeeze = LB/RB, menu = Start). SteamVR's Frame-to-Touch remap
folds right B, X and Y into one Touch button, the d-pad into two, and drops
the bumpers and the right menu. With OXRSYS_FRAME_XBOX set, the Touch A/B/X/Y
bits are rebuilt from the Frame client's per-input bits so each Frame letter
lands on the Xbox button of the same letter; the bumpers press the grips and
the right menu is MENU. A packet with no Frame bits is left alone, and the
Frame bits stay, so Frame-profile bindings still read their own inputs.
The left d-pad also reads under a non-Frame profile (dpad_*/click), which
UEVR binds through its own profile JSON.

First written for and worn in Sifu under UEVR, 2026-10-26.
Test: InputManager, OXRSYS_FRAME_XBOX puts each Frame letter on the same
Xbox letter under Touch.

